# Example 17-03: A real liveness failure with a cardinality counter
# Messages keep arriving and are acked one at a time. Nothing stops Send, so
# the backlog may never shrink to one: the counterexample alternates Send and
# Ack forever, which a real queue can do.
# Demonstrates: loops that increment are kept; only decrement-only loops are
# ignored.

action Init:
    pending = cardinality.counter(0)

atomic fair action Send:
    pending = pending.inc()

atomic fair action Ack:
    require not pending.is_zero()
    pending = oneof pending.dec()

always eventually assertion BacklogShrinks:
    return not pending.is_many()
